1
00:00:00,986 --> 00:00:03,276
(Penny:)-Aristotle?
-No.

2
00:00:03,697 --> 00:00:05,327
(Penny:)-Five?
-Oh!

3
00:00:05,657 --> 00:00:08,947
Oh, then I don't know.

4
00:00:10,286 --> 00:00:13,786
(Sheldon:)-Why are you crying?
-Because I'm stupid.

5
00:00:13,957 --> 00:00:16,037
Well, that's no reason to cry.

6
00:00:17,335 --> 00:00:19,255
No, one cries because one is sad.

7
00:00:19,421 --> 00:00:24,131
(Sheldon:)For example, I cry because
others are stupid and it makes me sad.

8
00:00:25,677 --> 00:00:28,677
(Penny:)Look, can we just please forget
about all this extra stuff...

9
00:00:28,847 --> 00:00:31,477
(Penny:)...and can you just tell me
what Leonard does?

10
00:00:31,641 --> 00:00:32,721
(Howard:)All right.

11
00:00:32,892 --> 00:00:35,432
(Sheldon:)Leonard is attempting to learn...

12
00:00:35,603 --> 00:00:38,193
(Sheldon:)...why subatomic particles
move the way they do.

13
00:00:39,190 --> 00:00:42,780
(Penny:)Really? That's it?
Well, that doesn't sound so complicated.

14
00:00:42,944 --> 00:00:46,154
(Sheldon:)It's not. That's why Leonard does it.

15
00:00:48,992 --> 00:00:50,872
(Penny:)Okay, I just have one question.

16
00:00:51,036 --> 00:00:53,576
(Penny:)What exactly are subatomic particles?

17
00:00:53,747 --> 00:00:56,627
(Sheldon:)-A good question.
-Thank you.

18
00:00:56,791 --> 00:01:00,021
(Sheldon:)And to answer it, we first must
ask ourselves, "What is physics?"

